Q2. Student Result System
Medium
Concept: Validation inside setters
Create a class named Student.
Private fields: name, rollNumber, marks.
Requirements:
- Set the student's name and roll number through a constructor.
- Marks must be between 0 and 100.
- Create setMarks(int marks) that updates marks only when valid.
- Create getMarks() to read marks.
- Create getGrade():
  - 90–100: A
  - 75–89: B
  - 60–74: C
  - 40–59: D
  - Below 40: Fail
- Invalid marks must not overwrite the previous valid marks.
Test: Set marks to 85, then try setting them to 120.
Think: Why should validation happen inside the class instead of relying on main()?
