Q3. Mobile Phone Settings
Medium
Concept: Read-only fields and controlled modification
Create a class named MobilePhone.
Private fields: brand, model, batteryPercentage, volume.
Requirements:
- Initialize all fields using a constructor.
- Battery must stay between 0 and 100.
- Volume must stay between 0 and 100.
- Create chargeBattery(int percentage) to increase battery.
- Battery must never exceed 100.
- Create changeVolume(int volume) with validation.
- Create getters for all fields.
- Brand and model must not be directly modifiable after object creation.
Test: Start with 70% battery and 30 volume. Charge by 50% and set volume to 80.
Think: Why is a controlled method better than a public variable?
